A||||10||Gokart||Exhaust Manifold question||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||03-22-2000||07:30 PM||||My GT is sounding like I have a exhaust leak lately and now I'm noticing a ticking sound louder than the noise the injectors puts out. Is there a sure fire way to tell if it's time to replace the exhaust manifold(s)? Any tests on them I can do? Eventually will it set off a code? TIA for replies!||||reg||5
Z||000001||mshill||03-22-2000||07:51 PM||||You won't see any code set.  If it gets worse, when you accelerate, it will start to sound like the old VW bug.<P>||||reg||9
Z||000002||batboy||03-22-2000||08:25 PM||||I have a manifold leak now on my 85GT, I asked the muffler shop to check out my exhaust system and when it was up on the rack, they showed me exactly where it was leaking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||03-22-2000||08:51 PM||||Thanks, I wasn't sure if Midas/Meineke could tell if a manifold was leaking. I'll swing by Saturday. Can anyone recommend the best replacement? Maybe one that will increase HP! If their is a crack, I'm not going to mess with having it welded.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||03-22-2000||09:59 PM||||My 85se v-6 made the classic tic-tic-tic noise.  When I pulled the engine to replace the clutch all I found wrong was a loose exhaust manifold bolt.  The manifolds were fine.  I did however port and re-weld them while I had them off.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Luperman||03-22-2000||11:03 PM||||I had a crack in my manifold welded ten years ago and it has'nt come back yet (fingers are still crossed)||||reg||10
Z||000006||JIM GOOSE||03-23-2000||07:38 AM||||If I were you , I would check the manifold bolts, they can get loose. When I did my engine work, I drilled and tapped these holes oversize to accept the studs commonly available(3/8", coarse thread on block side &fine-nut side). These are loctited into the head & holes in manf. adjusted to fit with clearance for exp/cont. However, the nuts would loosen from time to time so now have inst thin jam nuts on all of them. My manf have been ported ,welded ouside and cermet coated (88 v6 GT)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||03-23-2000||07:40 PM||||Got the wife convinced that if it is the manifold(s) leaking I should get the Fiero Stores Sprint manifolds ($550.00+)! Granted I can get the bolts off, is this swap fairly easy? Has anyone ever gotten these? Figure I'd always have them as long as I stick with the stock engine and/or get a 3.2 conversion someday!||||reg||14
Z||000008||sluppy123||03-23-2000||08:46 PM||||To find out where/if your manifold is leaking find yourself a length of small diameter hose 1/4-1/2" hold one end by your ear, the take the other end and probe around the manifold (with the engine running) be careful not to burn yourself or stick the tube in your ear  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||03-23-2000||10:05 PM||||Thanks for your help guys! After doing a "exhausting" search <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">I decided that money spent on Sprint manifolds wouldn't be worth it so I'm going to see about getting them ported/welded.||||reg||14
Z||000010||DXR_DAD||03-23-2000||10:14 PM||||Hum........I think I remember some other guy saying the same thing??? and as I remember he was very happy with the "port&weld". Can't think of his name ???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||14
